E.2 Abstention Criterion

The system abstains from recommending when:

\text{abstain} \iff \max_{a \in \mathcal{A}(b)} \left[ V_T(b \mid \text{do}(a)) - V_T(b) \right] < \delta_{\min}

where \delta_{\min} = 0.05 (5 percentage points in viability probability). This threshold is calibrated to the minimum clinically significant difference. A bad recommendation is worse than no recommendation.

When abstaining, the system returns:

```json
{
  "bottlenecks": [],
  "abstain": true,
  "abstain_reason": "No intervention meets the minimum effect threshold. Current viability: 0.12. Best intervention effect: 0.03 (below threshold 0.05).",
  "recommendation": "Consult with a human caseworker for personalized assessment."
}
```

